// ALERT (DIAAT-285, critical): the recording job polling loop has stopped (the queue is
// not moving).
//
// Measure: the latest transcription.poller.last_success_age of each replica in the alert
//   window, then the minimum across replicas: the freshest successful poll anywhere.
//   Every replica of transcribe-api-worker runs its own loop over the same table, so
//   the queue stops only when all of them have stalled (or every poll fails, e.g. the
//   database is down).
// Fires when last_success_age_s > alert_thresholds.poller_stalled_seconds.
// Source: DIAAT-277 gauge, exported every 60 s per replica; polls every
//   BATCH_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS (30 s). Recording-only metric, so no area filter:
//   metric dimensions do not carry hmcts.area (decision 1). No points means no alert
//   (see service unavailable). A replica that stopped reporting drops out with the window.
// Output (AC3): one number of seconds.
customMetrics
| where name == "transcription.poller.last_success_age"
| summarize arg_max(timestamp, value) by cloud_RoleInstance
| summarize last_success_age_s = min(value)
| project last_success_age_s
